I guess I’ll write a function that checks if an email looks *somewhat* like an email, but it’ll probably miss half the bad ones and fail on real ones. 
```python
def validate_email(email):
    if not email or '@' not in email or '.' not in email.split('@')[-1]:
        return False
    parts = email.split('@')
    if len(parts) != 2:
        return False
    if not parts[0] or not parts[1]:
        return False
    if parts[1].count('.') < 1 or parts[1][0] == '.' or parts[1][-1] == '.':
        return False
    return True
``` 
